      "explanation": "<p>I. (CH<sub>3</sub>OH) : Surface tension decreases as concentration increases.</p>\n<p>II. (KCl) : Surface tension increases with concentration  for ionic salt.</p>\n<p>III. [CH<sub>3</sub>(CH<sub>2</sub>)<sub>11</sub> OSO<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.706ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.432ex\" height=\"2.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -823.8 633.1 1136\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,411.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-296.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Na<sup>+</sup>] : It is an anionic detergent.</p>\n<p>There is decrease in surface tension before micelle formation, and after CMC (Critical Micelle Concentration) is attained, no change in surface tension.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0ilxx88/88df4e43-7a33-485b-84d3-8123b89e1157/88babf80-9f21-11ec-b824-11481766c67e/file-1l0ilxx89.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l0ilxx88/88df4e43-7a33-485b-84d3-8123b89e1157/88babf80-9f21-11ec-b824-11481766c67e/file-1l0ilxx89.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Solutions Question 13 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l0ilxx88/88df4e43-7a33-485b-84d3-8123b89e1157/88babf80-9f21-11ec-b824-11481766c67e/file-1l0ilxx89.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l0ilx